This project uses d-kuro/kirocc (https://github.com/d-kuro/kirocc),
Apache License 2.0, Copyright d-kuro, as a behavioral reference. The
following pieces are transcribed from kirocc v0.11.1 and carry that
license and attribution:

- the static Claude model table (internal/models/models.go)
- effort-level resolution for extended thinking (internal/models/effort.go)
- the `GET /v1/models` response envelope (internal/server/handlers.go)
- the AWS EventStream test frame builder (internal/testutil/testutil.go)
- JSON Schema sanitization rules (internal/reqconv/schema_sanitize.go)
- tool name mapping rules (internal/reqconv/tool_name_map.go)
- tool definition conversion and cache-point placement
  (internal/reqconv/tool_convert.go, internal/reqconv/cache_points.go)
- `<env>` block parsing for the current message
  (internal/reqconv/env_state.go)
- message normalization before history is built
  (internal/reqconv/message_normalizer.go)
- history-entry construction and request payload assembly, including
  system-prompt placement (internal/reqconv/history.go,
  internal/reqconv/build_payload.go)
- content extraction: message text, current-message image promotion, and
  tool-result/image conversion (internal/reqconv/content_text.go,
  internal/reqconv/content_scan.go, internal/reqconv/tool_results.go,
  internal/reqconv/images.go)
- the response translation state machine: max-tokens budgeting,
  stop-sequence filtering, thinking-tag parsing, and tool-call
  deduplication (internal/respconv/token_budget.go,
  internal/respconv/stop_sequence.go, internal/respconv/thinking_tags.go,
  internal/respconv/tool_calls.go), excluding the advisor, tool-search,
  and GPT drain paths
- tool-use fragment accumulation across stream frames
  (internal/kiroproto/tooluse.go)
- the Kiro runtime HTTP client and its retry backoff
  (internal/kiroclient/client.go, internal/kiroclient/backoff.go)
- upstream error classification (internal/kiroclient/aws_error.go)
- regression cases transcribed from kirocc tests: most are fixture cases
  under tests/fixtures/, named in each case's meta.json; a few are inline
  unit tests next to the code they exercise, named in a comment directly
  above the test (for example kiro.rs's minimal_payload_wire_shape and
  catalog.rs's resolves_aliases_dates_and_suffixes and
  effort_resolution_follows_model_enum)

Everything else is an independent implementation.

This exact file is duplicated, byte for byte, at
crates/kiro-trust-protocol/NOTICE and crates/kiro-trust-kiro/NOTICE and
crates/kiro-trust/NOTICE so each published crate carries it (Apache-2.0
section 4(d)); a test in each of those crates asserts the copy matches this
one.
